            2. How We Picked: Solubility, Flavor and Dose
          </h2>

          <p>
            We did not run a lab test or a coffee taste panel for this guide. The picks come from label analysis, published certifications and the very consistent pattern in buyer feedback about which powders mix well in coffee and which do not, the same approach set out on our <a href="/how-we-test/">how we test page</a>. Where we describe taste, clumping or texture, we are reporting what buyers widely say rather than claiming results of our own.
          </p>

          <p>
            The first test was how well the powder dissolves in the kind of coffee it is meant for. A collagen had to be marketed and widely reported as dissolving in hot liquids; a whey had to be an isolate, which disperses more cleanly than concentrate, with a short ingredient list. Second, we looked at flavor: an unflavored powder had to be neutral enough to disappear into coffee, and a flavored one had to be designed around coffee rather than a dessert flavor that clashes with it.
          </p>

          <p>
