              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                No. Heat denatures, or unfolds, whey proteins, which changes their texture and causes clumping, but it does not remove the amino acids your body uses. Cooking eggs or meat denatures protein in the same way, and digestion unfolds proteins anyway. The issue with whey in hot coffee is texture, not lost nutrition.
              </p>
